  "question": {
    "text": "What are the truth values of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> respectively, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> always speak the truth in any argument?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mi>F</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>F</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mi>T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, truth value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> and truth value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math><br /><br />So,&nbsp;<math><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></math> is always false, therefore&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are always true<br /><br />(since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>q</mi></math> is false only when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is true and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is false<math><mo>)</mo></math>"
  }
}